# target/ is the host's build output, compiled by whatever JDK the developer happens to have. Copying
# it in would let a stale or wrong-release jar win over the one the image builds from source.
target/
.mvn/
*.iml
.idea/

# The differential harness's unpacked OUTPUT — tens of megabytes of cases and answers, rebuilt by
# `node harness/js-side.cjs` and read by nobody but a person.
#
# harness/fixtures/ is deliberately NOT here: it is the frozen JavaScript answers themselves, it is
# committed, and this module's harness tests read it during `mvn package` in the image build. Excluding
# it would fail every build with a missing-fixture error.
harness/out/
